          "text": "Decrease, 50%"
        }
      ],
      "correct": "3",
      "solution": "**Given:**\n\nA fraction dfrac{3}{5} is decreased by dfrac{2}{5}. The resulting fraction is then increased by 20%.\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nNew Value = Original Value × (1 + Percentage Change)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nInitial Fraction = dfrac{3}{5}\n\nDecreased Fraction: dfrac{3}{5} - dfrac{2}{5} = dfrac{1}{5}\n\nIncreased by 20%: dfrac{1}{5} times (1 + 0.20) = dfrac{1}{5} times 1.20\n\n⇒ dfrac{1}{5} times 1.20 = dfrac{1.20}{5} = dfrac{6}{25}\n\nPercentage Change = dfrac{dfrac{6}{25} - dfrac{3}{5}}{dfrac{3}{5}} times 100\\%\n\n⇒ dfrac{dfrac{6}{25} - dfrac{15}{25}}{dfrac{3}{5}} times 100\\%\n\n⇒ dfrac{-9}{25} times dfrac{5}{3} times 100 %\n\n⇒ -60\\%\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option 3 i.e. decrease by 60%.**",
      "tags": [
        "Fractions"
      ]
